9,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YyJ8N","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333","html_url":"https://github.com/YYF233333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T03:49:39Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T03:49:39Z","body":"> What code is affected by this goto discrepancy?\r\n\r\n`GDScriptFunction::call`, see this part: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/99a8ab795d65e816ea7c452aa0fb55d02385c048/modules/gdscript/gdscript_vm.cpp#L230C1-L429C50\r\n\r\nSorry for my poor English, feel free to correct me 😄","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563284749/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563286359","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100838#issuecomment-2563286359","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100838","id":2563286359,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YyKVX","user":{"login":"SlashScreen","id":12375239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzc1MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12375239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen","html_url":"https://github.com/SlashScreen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T03:53:49Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T03:53:49Z","body":"Ah, right, I was going to figure out what that was for at some point. Should I get rid of it if I'm not using the switch opcode execute loop? \r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563286359/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563290743","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100838#issuecomment-2563290743","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100838","id":2563290743,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YyLZ3","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333","html_url":"https://github.com/YYF233333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T04:04:14Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T04:04:14Z","body":"If you have a completely different approach, just remove them all I think.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563290743/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563379128","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100838#issuecomment-2563379128","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100838","id":2563379128,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yyg-4","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T06:42:00Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T06:42:00Z","body":"I haven't reviewed this PR in detail and I'm not an expert in VMs, but I doubt this is a good change.\r\n\r\n1. We can't ignore performance considerations. VM is often a hot code path, we can't just say \"let's sacrifice some performance for readability, elegance and other formal metrics like function size\". As long as the code remains maintainable for us, we are willing to make any optimizations and \"ignore\" code style that would be unacceptable for normal code, since VM is a special case.\r\n2. I don't agree that splitting into multiple functions improves readability and maintainability for VMs. Each opcode is already isolated from the others, so we don't face typical FSM problems, a giant `switch` is not a problem.\r\n3. I don't think that reducing the number of opcodes is necessarily a good thing. For example, CPython has over 200 opcodes. Instead of a large number of opcodes, you get a lot of branching at runtime. While a larger number of opcodes allows you to avoid this and move some of the evaluations to the compilation stage. Yes, in return this leads to an increase in the code size, which can cause cache misses. But this requires careful measurements and balancing between the two extremes, there is no absolute good and absolute evil here.\r\n4. In my opinion, this change is also debatable from the point of view of readability. Instead of a large function with a simple structure, you get many smaller functions and enumerations. Also, the essence of the opcode becomes more complex, instead of a simple identifier, it now has arguments (in addition to the bytecode arguments).\r\n5. Macro magic is needed to use _computed goto_, which is not supported by all compilers.\r\n\r\nAs far as I know, the current VM organization corresponds to the generally accepted practices of organizing interpreters. Please read [The Design & Implementation of the CPython Virtual Machine](https://substack.com/@abhinavupadhyay/p-143567425), and you will find many similarities with the GDScript VM. The main difference is that CPython's source code is generated by scripts, while ours is written by hand, using a few macros.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563379128/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563409199","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100838#issuecomment-2563409199","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100838","id":2563409199,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YyoUv","user":{"login":"SlashScreen","id":12375239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzc1MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12375239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen","html_url":"https://github.com/SlashScreen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T07:26:48Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T07:26:48Z","body":"> We can't ignore performance considerations. \r\n\r\nI'm not. This was spawned from a [discussion in proposals](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/6031) about improving performance, and we determined the VM needs to be heavily modified, as well as optimizations in other parts of the compilation process. This is merely step 1 of that process to make it easier to work on. I personally want to rewrite the whole thing into a register machine to follow Lua, but we don't know if that's necessary yet, since it would take a lot of effort on my part.\r\n\r\n> I don't agree that splitting into multiple functions improves readability and maintainability for VMs.\r\n\r\nWe'll see. I found working within the main loop as it stands to be a mess that made me anxious, and I can't be the only one. \r\n\r\n>  For example, CPython has over 200 opcodes.\r\n\r\nThis assumes CPython is something we want to emulate. I don't think it's something to try to replicate, since we are trying to focus on performance.\r\n\r\n> Instead of a large number of opcodes, you get a lot of branching at runtime.\r\n\r\nI sort of agree here, but this is ignoring that my primary idea for the main loop would to index into an array of function pointers, rather than use a switch statement and then another switch statement inside the opcode functions. Hopefully in the future with a unified type system, a lot of the branching can be eliminated, since we would hopefully not need to switch on every primitive type.\r\n\r\n> Instead of a large function with a simple structure,\r\n\r\nAgain, the 3000-line behemoth is, in my view, much less approachable or easily navigable than a lot of smaller functions.\r\n\r\n>  Also, the essence of the opcode becomes more complex,\r\n\r\nI do agree here mostly, although I view it as another bytecode argument than added to the opcode. Not all of the opcodes have these arguments.\r\n\r\n> Macro magic is needed to use computed goto\r\n\r\nI don't want to use computed goto. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563409199/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":3,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563415856","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100838#issuecomment-2563415856","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100838","id":2563415856,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yyp8w","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T07:35:55Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T07:35:55Z","body":"Is there a good reason to do this refactoring that's visible to the user developers using Godot Engine?\r\n\r\nI only saw mention of a slight optimization. I would appreciate it if you could explain what benefits we would have.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563415856/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563429698","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100838#issuecomment-2563429698","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100838","id":2563429698,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YytVC","user":{"login":"SlashScreen","id":12375239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzc1MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12375239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen","html_url":"https://github.com/SlashScreen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlashScreen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T07:56:04Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T07:56:04Z","body":"The goal was not to be significantly visible to the end user, but rather to make it easier to change in the future as part of a several step process for improving GDScript performance by simplifying how it works internally, performing some basic code optimizations, and rethinking how types are represented internally to allow for more flexibility in the language, which would come in a serie